@flexiarg operator/verdict-carries-its-reason
@title The Operator's Verdict on an Agent Proposal Carries Its Reason
@status accepted 2026-11-11: proposed by 象 for 2 turns (Joe 2026-11-11: recurrence suffices); attested once used in a mission or a War Machine cascade
@provenance 象 proposals, ~/.emacs-graph/session-turn-analysis/<record>[.json].candidates.json; records: turn-STFTI2 turn-ZXN1KT
@parent apparatus/one-authority-per-question
@context The agent has proposed mappings, explorations, or a next-steps list; the operator answers each with a verdict.

! conclusion: Attach the reason to the verdict — authority ('we don't need to ask', I already know), constraint ('that's at a reasonable scale'), or prior reframing ('I've reframed it myself').

  + IF:
    The operator approves ('that's accurate… we don't need to ask', s1; 'I agree… best to work with the mark8 APM data', s5) or declines ('I'd decline that list as stated', s6).

  + HOWEVER:
    A bare verdict leaves the agent unable to update its model of the operator's criteria; the next proposal repeats the same miss.

  + THEN:
    Attach the reason to the verdict — authority ('we don't need to ask', I already know), constraint ('that's at a reasonable scale'), or prior reframing ('I've reframed it myself').

  + BECAUSE:
    One-authority-per-question gives each question exactly one source of truth; the operator IS that authority for his own work, and the attached reason is what makes the verdict reusable rather than a bare bit. Covers fragments s1, s5, s6.
